# Store credentials. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is ignored by git and must stay that way. These values are a write
# credential for a bucket.
#
# The secret exists in exactly three places:
#
#   1. Vercel environment variables — production and preview separate — for the
#      presign endpoint, which is the only deployed thing that reads it.
#      Created as Secret (write-only), which the edge runtime reads fine.
#      Note the names are case-sensitive. See docs/deploying.md.
#   2. GitHub Actions secrets, for anything CI publishes.
#   3. .env.local, on a developer's machine.
#
# Nowhere else. The opener and the desktop app upload through a short-lived
# presigned URL and never see a key; the edge middleware reads public sidecars;
# reads are public throughout. A credential in a browser bundle is readable by
# whoever was sent the link.
#
# The R2 API token is scoped to the one bucket, object read/write only, one per
# environment.

# --- A directory, for a local test or a machine that serves its own files -----
# DAI_STORE_DIR=./store
# The URL that directory appears under. Without it, links name a file: URL that
# only this machine can follow — right for a test, useless to send.
# DAI_STORE_BASE=https://store.example/

# --- The bucket ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Set all five or none. A part-configured store refuses to publish rather than
# quietly writing somewhere else.
# DAI_STORE_ENDPOINT=https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# DAI_STORE_BUCKET=dai-store
# DAI_STORE_REGION=auto
# DAI_STORE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# DAI_STORE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Where the public reads the bucket: the custom domain, not the endpoint.
# DAI_STORE_PUBLIC_BASE=https://store.opendai.app/

# Accept documents stored without encryption. Off unless this is a store you run
# inside a perimeter that already controls who reaches it — with it on, the store
# can read every document it holds, and so can anything between.
# DAI_STORE_ALLOW_CLEAR=0

# --- The presign endpoint -----------------------------------------------------
# How many uploads one address may start per hour, and the largest object it
# will hand out a URL for. Both have defaults; set them to tighten.
# DAI_PRESIGN_PER_HOUR=20
# DAI_PRESIGN_MAX_BYTES=5242880

# --- The MCP server -----------------------------------------------------------
# Where links point.
# DAI_OPENER=https://opendai.app
# Turn link previews off by default for every app this server builds.
# DAI_PREVIEW_DEFAULT=off
